-- NEWER VGM Other Games — Activision Blizzard / Vivendi Universal / Sierra Entertainment
--
-- Source: reference/NEWER VGM Sound Sources - Other Games.csv lines 25-568.
-- ~40 game records, ~520 usage rows.
--
-- Third Other Games batch. Sprawling western publisher catalogue spanning
-- 1996 Diablo through 2020 Call of Duty: Black Ops - Cold War. Heavy
-- composer credit coverage. Spyro Reignited Trilogy (2018 remaster) has
-- three sub-game-records for the original PS1 trilogy entries, since
-- the CSV documents each remake's source samples separately.
--
-- Composer credits applied (from in-CSV "(Music by:" notes):
--   - Diablo                              — Matt Uelmen
--   - THPS 1 + 2                          — Brian Bright
--   - Toy Story 2 + Crash Wrath of Cortex — Andy Blythe, Marten Joustra
--   - Spider-Man (PSX)                    — Tommy Tallarico, Howard Ulyate
--   - Simpsons Wrestling + Futurama       — Christopher Tyng
--   - Spider-Man 2: Enter Electro         — Todd Masten
--   - Crash Huge Adventure                — Manfred Linzner, Todd Masten
--   - Spyro: Enter the Dragonfly          — Stewart Copeland
--   - Crash Nitro Kart                    — Ashif Hakik, Todd Masten
--   - Simpsons Hit & Run                  — Marc Baril, Jeff Tymoschuk, Allan Levy
--   - Crash Purple + Spyro Orange         — Martin Schioeler
--   - World of Warcraft                   — Jason Hayes
--   - X-Men Legends                       — Rik Schaffer
--   - Spyro: A Hero's Tail                — Guy Cockcroft, Steve Duckworth, Keith Leary
--   - Crash Tag Team Racing               — Marc Baril, Spiralmouth, Michael Neilson
--   - Legend of Spyro: A New Beginning    — Rebecca Kneubuhl, Gabriel Mann, Noel Gabriel (DS), Mark Yeend (DS)
--   - Crash of the Titans                 — Marc Baril
--   - Legend of Spyro: Eternal Night      — Gabriel Mann, Rebecca Kneubuhl (console), Tom Miller (portable)
--   - CoD: Black Ops                      — Sean Murray
--   - CoD: Black Ops II                   — Jack Wall, Jimmy Hinson, Sergio Jimenez Lacima,
--                                            Shawn Jimmerson, James McCawley, Kevin Sherwood, Brian Tuey
--   - CoD: Black Ops III / IIII / Cold War — Jack Wall
--
-- Composer NULL (Rule 2 — no in-CSV credit) for:
--   The Mummy Returns, THPS 3, 3-D Ultra Pinball Thrillride, Spider-Man (2002),
--   Spider-Man 2 (2004), Tony Hawk's Underground 2, Shrek: Ogres & Dronkeys,
--   Crash: Mind Over Mutant, Call Of Duty: World At War, Overwatch,
--   Crash Bandicoot N. Sane Trilogy, Spyro Reignited Trilogy (+ sub-records),
--   Crash Team Racing Nitro-Fueled.
--
-- Spyro Reignited Trilogy split:
--   CSV row 482 is the Reignited Trilogy umbrella; rows 483/491/527 are
--   sub-headers for "Spyro the Dragon", "Spyro 2: Ripto's Rage!", and
--   "Spyro: Year of the Dragon" — each treated as a distinct game record
--   "Spyro Reignited Trilogy: <title>" to disambiguate from the original
--   PS1 games (which will appear in the Sony section batch).
--
-- New manufacturers introduced this batch:
--   - Data Becker & Masterbits     (composite — Sound Clips 10,000)
--   - EastWest & Chronic Music     (composite — L.A. Riot 3)
--   - Ninja Tune                   (Coldcut - Playtime)
--   - Audio Adventures Inc.        (Symphonic Adventures)
--   - Sonic Arts                   (Sounds of the 70's)
--   - Sonic Reality                (American Heartland)
--   - Casio                        (MT- — unknown vintage Casio keytar/sampler)
--   - Garritan                     (GigaHarp)
--   - Sampleheads                  (Whole Lotta Country)
--   - Q Up Arts                    (distinct from existing "Q-Up Arts" per Rule 2)
--   - ILIO                         (Ethno Techno)
--   - Sonic Foundry & Sounds Good  (composite — Methods Of Mayhem - Industrial Toolkit)
--   - Image-Line                   (FL Studio, Harmor)
--   - Ninevolt Audio               (Action Drums)
--   - Universal Production Music   (Too Much Fun)
--   - InSession Audio              (Smokin' Country Guitar)
--   - 8Dio                         (New Rhythmic Aura 1)
--   - Sonokinetic                  (Sultan Strings)
--   - Black Octopus                (Leviathan)
--   - Zenhiser                     (TRANCE BLISS)
--   - EZdrummer 3                  (CSV row 439 lists "EZdrummer 3" as manufacturer
--                                   with "Superior Drummer 2" as product — appears to be
--                                   contributor confusion between Toontrack products;
--                                   preserved verbatim per Rule 2)
--
-- Verbatim preservations (Rule 2 / Rule 11):
--   - "Tony Hawk's Underground 2" — title uses typographic right
--     single quote (U+2019), not ASCII apostrophe. Preserved.
--   - "Spectrasonics Metamorphosis" (Spider-Man 2 Enter Electro T80 +
--     Spyro: Enter the Dragonfly T137-143) is distinct from existing
--     "Metamorphosis S.A.G.E. Xpander" — new product per Rule 2.
--   - "Spectrasonics Burning Grooves" (Spyro: Year of the Dragon T529)
--     is distinct from existing "Burning Grooves S.A.G.E. Xpander"
--     (Rhythm Thief batch) — new product per Rule 2.
--   - "Native Instruments Kontakt" (CoD World at War T406) is distinct
--     from existing "Kontakt Factory Library" — new product per Rule 2.
--   - "Q Up Arts" (Legend of Spyro: A New Beginning T317) is distinct
--     from existing "Q-Up Arts" (Star Fox Adventures, Rare batch).
--     Hyphen vs space — strings differ.
--   - "AMG 160db - The Drum&Bass Interface" (Futurama T159-162) uses
--     lowercase "160db"; the existing Rhythm Thief product is "160dB"
--     with capital B. Strings differ — preserved as distinct.
--   - "Call of Duty: Black Ops IIII" — official capitalization of
--     Black Ops 4 (release title used Roman-style "IIII" branding).
--   - Casio "MT-" product name with trailing dash and ellipsis is a
--     contributor placeholder for an unidentified model in the MT series;
--     preserved verbatim.

